; kind id x y, in tiles, then any settings. Exits and triggers are rectangles from their top left tile.
[objects]
spawn start 9.5 9 facing=down
spawn gate 9.5 9 facing=down
exit questeria 8 6 w=4 to=questeria at=east-gate

; The east gate, in the wall. Its way through is the road between its towers; the way back into
; the city is the dark of its arch.
prop east-gate 9.5 10.75
prop city-wall 1.75 5.5
prop city-wall 17.25 5.5

; The city's gardens behind the wall, the tops of their cypresses showing over it.
prop cypress 1.4 3.2
prop cypress 2.8 2.6
prop cypress 16.9 2.8
prop cypress 18.5 3.4

; The Watch on the gate, Brisk in front of it, and the mother and her child begging him. They're
; all still here after the raid; they've more to say then.
scene a1-c3-01 9.5 11 talk=a1-c3-01 when=a1-c2-04 unless=a1-c3-01
npc brisk 11.4 12.4 cast=brisk facing=left
npc watch-a 6.8 11.6 cast=watch facing=down say="Orders from the Chancellor. Nobody comes in.|Step back from the gate, please.|I don't like it either. Doesn't change it."
npc watch-b 12.6 11.4 cast=watch facing=down say="Sickness or spies, they say. Look at them.|Half the Watch is in Greywatch. We can't hold a crowd.|Keep it moving."
npc refugee-mother 9.6 14.2 cast=refugee-mother facing=up
npc refugee-child 8.5 14.6 cast=refugee-child facing=up

; The camp, swollen overnight: tents pitched wherever there was room, cooking fires between them,
; bundles left where people dropped, and in the middle Mira's table, with the sick on cots round it
; and the supplies she's been sent stacked by it.
